    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭtūmĭno</span></b> ,
			āre, 1, v. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				cover</i> or <i>impregnate with bitumen</i> (late
			Lat.), Ambros. Hexaëm. 6, 9, 72; cf.: bitumino, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσφαλτόω</span>, Gloss. Lab.—Hence,
				<i>P. a.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭtū-mĭnătus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>impregnated with
			bitumen</i>, <i>bituminous</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 6, 32, § 59</span></i>
			.</div>
